[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3edafb7e-5a8e-568e-93a2-d9776a6084b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562864} {:answer/id #uuid "f014b7fd-ab32-5bb4-a516-8d9a267ee4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f014b7fd-ab32-5bb4-a516-8d9a267ee4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562916} :answer-field/id #uuid "b19a20c5-afb7-5dc2-9fc1-9c594316a164" :answer-field/key "The product $RS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5bd226a-d5ac-511a-968f-be677f0cb766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562910} {:answer/id #uuid "f32f88d7-1c04-5ee9-8f63-bdecfc1ed874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5bd226a-d5ac-511a-968f-be677f0cb766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562910} :answer-field/id #uuid "be555373-045c-506a-8a35-eea9aaaa8935" :answer-field/key "The product $PR$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "731763ab-ecfa-5d9f-b97e-e57ab7f3ac3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562879} {:answer/id #uuid "809c9224-decc-5959-8d36-bdbe575f61bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "809c9224-decc-5959-8d36-bdbe575f61bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562883} :answer-field/id #uuid "c974abcf-7262-5f9f-bd6b-6da19ef7805f" :answer-field/key "The product $PS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dae7e456-3839-5dcb-895a-6ba2eaf143b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575691} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd4e8b2-7813-593a-9dd2-483f48985aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fd4e8b2-7813-593a-9dd2-483f48985aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575695} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f26866-b872-5098-a81f-fd83d23a141a" :answer-field/key "None of these products is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fe7d2e4-659c-5b6e-9c9b-6d0a9162b9e8" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -5 & -8 & -8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector. \n\nThere are $5$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $RS$, $PS$, and $PR$ are undefined. Select “None of these products is well defined.”"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "634eda15-ac4c-58ee-8987-5a03c7951b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562876} {:answer/id #uuid "fab3f125-4732-5852-8a3b-74a036577c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fab3f125-4732-5852-8a3b-74a036577c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562919} :answer-field/id #uuid "002a391d-196d-5e6e-a5ad-c8c4da7a9101" :answer-field/key "The product $PS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07fe8f3f-cc9a-59da-b696-08b8234d657b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562855} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7178d2-bc56-574e-b59d-1437513c672c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd7178d2-bc56-574e-b59d-1437513c672c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562900} :answer-field/id #uuid "c81cfd27-3d9f-55aa-bdd4-33c537434f5d" :answer-field/key "The product $RS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b523942-a4cc-52af-ac57-78219e1b3443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562886} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8f128a-f61f-5456-8848-2ff32e232e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b523942-a4cc-52af-ac57-78219e1b3443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562886} :answer-field/id #uuid "d17b4073-f034-57d1-9612-84b24201e0f5" :answer-field/key "The product $SP$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8df2d590-e8b0-5a5d-8213-fe14bd38e587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575692} {:answer/id #uuid "2231559b-1dda-5d04-906a-ad2d568dd30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2231559b-1dda-5d04-906a-ad2d568dd30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575696} :answer-field/id #uuid "1186e35f-50a9-53ca-ba43-b49a2e3d114b" :answer-field/key "None of these products is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e01af3ae-fb4a-5e38-8b42-8320c8e0b105" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ -7 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 & -9 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $5$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $SP$, $PS$, and $RS$ are undefined. Select “None of these products is well defined.”"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33cabe4d-81d5-5ae5-a052-6b0f90339d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563947} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2ceec3-2f3e-5f8a-af31-4bf0d30583a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33cabe4d-81d5-5ae5-a052-6b0f90339d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563947} :answer-field/id #uuid "343ee5cc-167e-5420-8b88-ea96eee350c3" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16436961-67f5-507a-8527-cfd7be7c22f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563946} {:answer/id #uuid "391abf30-e9c8-5c80-9cec-05a5f3751aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16436961-67f5-507a-8527-cfd7be7c22f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563946} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f0e32b1-d7c9-5fb8-890f-83bcffc9c539" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85b42d95-12ac-5561-8a12-a148b416989e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563953} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3a70a1-2772-5e12-9e1e-3be31b98e9fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc3a70a1-2772-5e12-9e1e-3be31b98e9fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563955} :answer-field/id #uuid "829c0450-9cce-5651-b5b3-bdafd9e37e3c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a540170-78c2-57d7-83ad-e1402d5fe8aa" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a688cf79790cde240a1fabeb768a9500c98e7affc1006c39e35b89582627fb0c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the elliptic arc is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion.\n\n![](images/dc/dcc2f364085ccca85e6e6ddd8a5affac51c84f774281b817d4852bd2322bcb1b.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ the force is still perpendicular to the motion.\n\n![](images/50/508e0ac5f67d7b119ad689ccaede8894268eefe31d9b00f148ddd6bf851de6b4.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "300fad0e-fd42-55a8-89ea-fd53b94738a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564862} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb4e3d9-c68d-5d96-b2ca-e83a0ec8f365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eb4e3d9-c68d-5d96-b2ca-e83a0ec8f365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564887} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a756679-ef95-5ead-ac0c-59325a180803" :answer-field/key "At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a00f9c7c-eb2e-534f-96d9-21f5d55d8e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564893} {:answer/id #uuid "e51414ea-9ddc-56ea-b7da-1ed3610556b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e51414ea-9ddc-56ea-b7da-1ed3610556b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564918} :answer-field/id #uuid "6995f8c6-a759-5950-9349-963ca5de09e3" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758c0564-deae-52c8-b5b3-c47827255183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564881} {:answer/id #uuid "b707bcbb-75bb-5476-bbd6-45f627b422ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "758c0564-deae-52c8-b5b3-c47827255183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564881} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fa5f12c-832f-57ec-a592-7f5244b29e13" :answer-field/key "At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02cbb13a-a6d7-5c1c-8f40-eee3ed956640" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-9x$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-9x.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0.$ In each open quadrant, $x$ has a fixed nonzero sign. The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/83/8306880f3f6b3d936d1e690cf75eb9e1a999f5b1c914d10c1886296317664fbe.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}]