} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4a105b-ceb3-5369-a285-0eb8ccce9659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef4a105b-ceb3-5369-a285-0eb8ccce9659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f521ac1c-ccfd-5b5e-851c-0d50cbcbf7a4" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0310b6c3-7a71-5e78-8f0c-a9029c12ce0c" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIn an open quadrant, each squared coordinate is positive, so the remaining coordinate factors and coefficient determine the sign.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ec462e2ce1055ca352de84813bc6d72731d74f93d44a1513b1dc284b504cb0b.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1105e5e5-56fb-57f9-b39f-9e424103ba6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564851} {:answer/id #uuid "dad633eb-7036-5a3c-932a-8be4dfc9a78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1105e5e5-56fb-57f9-b39f-9e424103ba6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564851} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4b8fd3-63c9-59c8-b5b9-961a488ace29" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/r