lution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 8 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-8\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 16 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=- 8 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 16 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5 y}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\not\\equiv - 40 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=- 8 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c669eed-d1b3-5024-8bdb-7d4214af06fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577243} {:answer/id #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" :