swer/id #uuid "aa042d30-52ac-50a2-a9aa-5b4841ae1d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dadf822-8f9a-5e65-ab38-5c493b2f2af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577258} :answer-field/id #uuid "e98f4f9d-447e-58a2-86b5-8024aca227a8" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{3 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 5 x^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 10 x.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 5 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-5\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 10 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=- 5 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 10 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\not\\equiv - 15 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=- 5 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=- 10 x.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e2d78a6-0098-5570-8b75-9658bac896ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577262} {:answer/id #uuid "923779fe-8a1d-5656-8015-eaf792fb0480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2d78a6-0098-5570-8b75-9658bac896ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577262} :answer-field/id #uuid "32dbae71-0c96-559b-b891-eaff9a25935a" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=- 8 x^{3}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a723154a-a31d-503b-9579-bae0b8ee2011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577266} {:answer/id #uuid "cee2c378-b3ae-5d85-ae7e-47e9f7d4b976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a723154a-a31d-503b-9579-bae0b8ee2011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577266} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f35dba7-7b86-5c82-83c0-dbf58e502ebf" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a265d0d-ea0d-51d2-a212-2a4111ec6a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577261} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f9d0a1-d778-50ce-98ec-358bbfec63d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a265d0d-ea0d-51d2-a212-2a4111ec6a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577261} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5666fa9-c3aa-5e43-b2c8-bbc511366f41" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "729ec480-d7e2-58dc-a850-b9ff69610ca0" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{4 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 x^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 8 x^{3}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 x^{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot 4 x^{3} \\\\ &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=- 2 x^{4}$ and $y\\prime=- 8 x^{3}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=- 2 x^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=- 8 x^{3}.$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc0976d-8848-5bc7-a8ba-c6fb66573dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577288} {:answer/id #uuid "91cca939-abfa-579c-ba0f-76aed088ff08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cca939-abfa-579c-ba0f-76aed088ff08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577306} :answer-field/id #uuid "9baa3746-90cb-500b-8251-3017a1530a1d" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbb8d0f-0fc7-5f97-8c4c-958d8e7cec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577317} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7030f3-f3be-5e06-ba36-6216c88dadef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acbb8d0f-0fc7-5f97-8c4c-958d8e7cec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577317} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4198222-2cf0-53fa-a803-9c2fa7bab7c3" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112c328d-2c2a-5fc0-b7ee-7c0fdc2ad74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577283} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4cc2d0-e201-5801-b07a-6b913c46b3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4cc2d0-e201-5801-b07a-6b913c46b3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577316} :answer-field/id #uuid "e49426b3-4b2b-5454-8130-574f46902c18" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}},\\qquad 3 x + 2>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)})/(-2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-\\ln(3 x + 2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac82169-4017-5aee-b8a2-b79e679b0722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577295} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1fbee2-4889-5e84-9f46-037cf43d3d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ac82169-4017-5aee-b8a2-b79e679b0722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577295} :answer-field/id #uuid "4712b020-9702-5c3c-a3ff-cabe5f1d6dfc" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d576c80-7571-50d0-bc26-368ad4cb8fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577286} {:answer/id #uuid "42fb3203-d6f2-5685-9a07-82e33c2e8163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42fb3203-d6f2-5685-9a07-82e33c2e8163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577289} :answer-field/id #uuid "61085ad0-ae6c-5fc4-974f-fb93aeef646c" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ad3c8a-d899-5f30-9f69-f2953849fa2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577309} {:answer/id #uuid "9abd5e60-f344-53f9-9b87-6cfd5386e6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99ad3c8a-d899-5f30-9f69-f2953849fa2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577309} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3ad4a5-9e8c-538b-8578-c03c5ca4643c" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a098865b-a0f4-5d9b-a304-bd75a306b510" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=6 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}},\\qquad 4 x + 4>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=3\\cdot\\frac{4}{4 x + 4} \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}6 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{12}{4 x + 4} &\\overset{?}{=}6e^{-(3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)})/(3)} \\\\ \\frac{12}{4 x + 4} &\\overset{?}{=}6e^{-\\ln(4 x + 4)} \\\\ \\frac{12}{4 x + 4} &\\not\\equiv \\frac{3}{2 \\left(x + 1\\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06be9c0a-0223-57ac-aa2a-f18ff8de1f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577280} {:answer/id #uuid "6d228363-cf1a-5ff6-9768-677aa5961cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d228363-cf1a-5ff6-9768-677aa5961cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577300} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d72eff3-71f9-5ab8-bb2e-d070834ba15b" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182d1adb-f26c-5500-ab80-039d7a4be356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/v