nt :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1365b427-e993-5bd4-86d1-0c5aa81651d0" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $1\\times 1$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $E$ has $2$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times$\n\n- The matrix $F$ has $1$ row and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 1.$ $\\,\\checkmark$\n\n- The matrix $G$ has $1$ row and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 1.$ $\\,\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, only $F$ and $G$ are $1\\times 1$ matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19755296-1ceb-5b2e-9297-0bd1e985df1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618937} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd96d2c-c257-5c70-bfe7-9e0253e913d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19755296-1ceb-5b2e-9297-0bd1e985df1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618937} :answer-field/id #uuid "58d92de7-8c90-5649-80fb-25c64c992660" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 8 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae41e8b0-9439-5da8-8a55-dd2847be9f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618958} {:answer/id #uuid "beff1b27-8897-5a64-aafd-6d0da94d5b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beff1b27-8897-5a64-aafd-6d0da94d5b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618965} :answer-field/id #uuid "61e90628-8659-5dad-abd4-5ec7206f32e0" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & -3 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf669b71-6cf4-5a20-8bbe-f28195f37ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618966} {:answer/id #uuid "e55041c1-182f-5c4b-97c1-6bf3c709743e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf669b71-6cf4-5a20-8bbe-f28195f37ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618966} :answer-field/id #uuid "733621ec-7e17-55ee-9a4d-ad47c13316e0" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3143678b-b430-5f13-b425-340f8d0b0484" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & -3 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since coefficient row $1$ contains only zeros, but row $3$ is nonzero (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $1$ is to the left of the leading entry in row $1$, column $2$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 8 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $A$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df7a3df9-ef94-5fda-bbc3-4d706dc7a7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618971} {:answer/id #uuid "eda4d7a5-d72a-5965-88b2-9759fab0577d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda4d7a5-d72a-5965-88b2-9759fab0577d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618976} :answer-field/id #uuid "85102761-4cff-52f1-9a8b-699f68189d0a" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 6 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 10 & -5 & 10\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e13ed20-c95d-5671-9538-ac896de3da03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618939} {:answer/id #uuid "f6660f11-1357-535d-ac53-922231277937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6660f11-1357-535d-ac53-922231277937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618978} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7a24be0-80e5-5062-bdf3-7961ae7b3f30" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e040d59-cd9d-53fd-ae26-6d8f5c7c8188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618938} {:answer/id #uuid "864d761e-726e-5907-b36c-796ede19fe25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "864d761e-726e-5907-b36c-796ede19fe25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618954} :answer-field/id #uuid "fab46e94-f4a3-508d-b7a4-b0ea3b3d83b7" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & -5 & 11 & 11 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 & -9\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "561ac9d8-2c57-5f24-a4da-1b32d54e7eb8" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $2$ is in the same column as the leading entry in row $1$, column $2$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 6 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 10 & -5 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & -5 & 11 & 11 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $B$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b511d614-a32a-5f2e-8982-862f2f8bc969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618960} {:answer/id #uuid "f87434c1-2715-5dbb-aef1-28b0ae4e63f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b511d614-a32a-5f2e-8982-862f2f8bc969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618960} :answer-field/id #uuid "086f4a75-a01f-5011-87f5-e49f49b9a1a7" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9530c90b-619f-583f-a521-7686913b18b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618956} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf4aad3-aced-55b5-82b2-4065bf09bcdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9530c90b-619f-583f-a521-7686913b18b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618956} :answer-field/id #uuid "3130e52f-ccc4-558c-9568-90fd403b7fb2" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 4 & 10 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 11 & 11 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 & 4\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8734e28-ad5f-5a91-ae22-2028f420ee18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618974} {:answer/id #uuid "f36ed341-06b7-58e0-a9b8-7bac32141be3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8734e28-ad5f-5a91-ae22-2028f420ee18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618974} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbdc51bc-b472-5961-a516-54460948c303" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 5 & 10\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b32d6bad-7619-5a20-9b5f-d26342503b3d" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $1$ is to the left of the leading entry in row $1$, column $2$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 4 & 10 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 11 & 11 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since coefficient row $2$ contains only zeros, but row $3$ is nonzero (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since coefficient row $2$ contains only zeros, but row $3$ is nonzero (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 5 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the matrices should be selected."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9603c309-38ce-52a7-a03f-396d1248e7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618957} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1fb287-0fcf-5bdf-b04c-1e76f5a04746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb1fb287-0fcf-5bdf-b04c-1e76f5a04746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618968} :answer-field/id #uuid "372d8bc2-42aa-5249-bc59-f40155356480" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & -4 & 2 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "187a1e0c-bc0a-5a2a-9322-5d6a9645059f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618936} {:answer/id #uuid "c05c93ce-7528-52cf-8cff-f7bc6c4b0bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "187a1e0c-bc0a-5a2a-9322-5d6a9645059f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618936} :answer-field/id #uuid "7be5a164-39f9-5011-bda8-ac28fca1ee4d" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f535fca-1ac5-5d7c-96ad-7f2ce62a3e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618947} {:answer/id #uuid "bde76bcf-c861-57b4-80b8-373546cc1d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f535fca-1ac5-5d7c-96ad-7f2ce62a3e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618947} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba11a20e-6817-558e-8a9c-8d559feca74f" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 9 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f76fef32-60e3-573d-88b2-f0a2a78f5139" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & -4 & 2 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $1$ is to the left of the leading entry in row $1$, column $2$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 9 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $A$, $B$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "531a4030-c66f-58d5-a359-012bc46b8f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619002} {:answer/id #uuid "94026d9d-2826-5c2a-8ff7-dd0db156e038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94026d9d-2826-5c2a-8ff7-dd0db156e038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619014} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e9ed11d-ce27-54db-a6a3-e8dda19a169c" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619018} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daf0364a-a566-5707-8969-d1c463b19c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619032} {:answer/id #uuid "e69af3c1-6b1e-5d09-86cc-96341ebfc12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e69af3c1-6b1e-5d09-86cc-96341ebfc12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619037} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddce10a9-700f-5512-9eaf-6c8e706f0c7c" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c915d88-2e11-5c90-8a2e-bef8d13e1924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619017} {:answer/id #uuid "ad284a24-e866-58b6-8b6b-c92774ec9a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad284a24-e866-58b6-8b6b-c92774ec9a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619020} :answer-field/id #uuid "f00270b5-88d5-57de-8ec6-5e4a504e67d3" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -3 & 7 \\\\ -9 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12be4e7e-490f-5ebf-b05f-bec415d51350" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $c_{21}=-9$ is in the same column as the leading entry $c_{11}=9$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -3 & 7 \\\\ -9 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #u