ains the nonpositive real numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\nTherefore, select none of the sets; leave every box unchecked."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b4c276-acb1-5d8a-94ef-d87e46aafb4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624666} {:answer/id #uuid "16b6b1bf-2448-51d2-bde4-c769ae4a4b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16b6b1bf-2448-51d2-bde4-c769ae4a4b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624676} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1fd2c2d-d6de-5db5-9476-1e3ef060b2da" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbb{Q}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0951f355-f617-53c5-9c1c-e8a6bd833a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624669} {:answer/id #uuid "815cb232-e680-50c6-b4ba-34d32aeb032e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "815cb232-e680-50c6-b4ba-34d32aeb032e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624704} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3c922da-a959-5376-bc48-006e912a7029" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbb{R}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "586a9db5-46fa-537f-a5f8-2b8c24442360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624692} {:answer/id #uuid "ab61ec59-c316-5197-9c30-fc67c5fa3e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586a9db5-46fa-537f-a5f8-2b8c24442360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624692} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7288dd3-d853-5c47-9699-691b00a2f5ce" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbb{Z}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ad7a74c-ef53-5710-9f82-a8aad9965b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624684} {:answer/id #uuid "a92e0627-2e68-588d-9eaa-2a8c231ef551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a92e0627-2e68-588d-9eaa-2a8c231ef551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624711} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc3716d7-04a2-5389-9da9-eaccd9006882" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbb{C}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c555e324-72f5-52a6-b605-665b3e814810" :question/problem "To which of the following sets do all the integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We must check whether each set contains all the integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}$ contains all rational numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{C}$ contains all complex numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{C}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{Q}$, $\\mathbb{C}$, $\\mathbb{Z}$, $\\mathbb{R}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203c3a72-98e4-5bba-8d52-643b5a8ae662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624804} {:answer/id #uuid "b734bbd4-ed56-5dd6-a26c-7063e1357dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "203c3a72-98e4-5bba-8d52-643b5a8ae662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624804} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ab60df-3af2-58f5-9cef-c78292566527" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "339a46f2-957b-50bf-81f3-f48099bbef4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624807} {:answer/id #uuid "60a8e9ca-aafe-5894-9859-ede2c8e74204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "339a46f2-957b-50bf-81f3-f48099bbef4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624807} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7eb9ed-f763-5a49-9c82-711b69bc3254" :answer-field/key "$y=4-2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c19a8dd4-fec8-5e9e-a375-1d5d1177cb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624831} {:answer/id #uuid "e144ef3a-7749-5b80-99ed-efa4e654d75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e144ef3a-7749-5b80-99ed-efa4e654d75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624841} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6cf20e0-1e2c-58bb-8d8a-40b535d8f986" :answer-field/key "$y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4348104f-2ff2-50b3-adec-adfa89f62726" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4fac094a684d7209071c624ffe184184d34d3b3439ade505555c5ecb1cbc2a02.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(2,3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/92/92b2d2e714fce68ca3b8a38d1ba35d8b35971d3bbb2a238d7d68f48042b8aa3c.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) &=- \\frac{1}{2}(0)+4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3) &=- \\frac{1}{2}(2)+4 \\\\ 3 &=3\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=4-2x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) &=4-2(0) \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3) &=4-2(2) \\\\ 3 &=0\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=4-2x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(0) &=4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2) &=4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4$, $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61947825-5d54-5e7d-86aa-4fdacf87166d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624815} {:answer/id #uuid "94eee39d-1fc4-5541-b921-57ac88c96add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94eee39d-1fc4-5541-b921-57ac88c96add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624823} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a299467-705e-530a-bc23-2edf622f4969" :answer-field/key "$y-2x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a7de2e-de37-52b1-8e53-d8cc7e9f7b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624802} {:answer/id #uuid "d62fbe1d-e009-5b52-8668-719abb430adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13a7de2e-de37-52b1-8e53-d8cc7e9f7b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624802} :answer-field/id #uuid "d624f006-00aa-5d70-a8db-84dd45b0ec04" :answer-field/key "$y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624837} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3005dfe8-0e56-5e72-91d5-ddfd6d576f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624806} {:answer/id #uuid "ade68938-8e0c-5bec-b216-bed7d6ad0c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3005dfe8-0e56-5e72-91d5-ddfd6d576f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624806} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8356280-4710-526b-8d59-c96daa96c3eb" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b254416d-e106-5d67-a907-672177ee0801" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efe35f51fa4ce8707e2ac4ce1785ece55e9191bcedbe2b22ff64b5e4510eb5c7.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-2)$ and $(2,-1)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/ac/ace116847d9b31abeb947a1e3952dc9f6aea7224602d394d9318efc51476bc6e.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2) &=\\frac{1}{2}(0)-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=\\frac{1}{2}(2)-2 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2) &=-2+\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=-2+\\frac{1}{2}(2) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y-2x=-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)-2(0) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1)-2(2) &=-2 \\\\ -5 &=-2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y-2x=-2$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2$, $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "433dc4d1-a082-5006-8b88-eea429c9c826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624809} {:answer/id #uuid "73a6fa18-cc12-592c-aa0f-ebeaef416a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a6fa18-cc12-592c-aa0f-ebeaef416a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624820} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae03a63-2324-5f95-b1f9-4b8e3ccf92c4" :answer-field/key "$2y-\\frac{4}{3}x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1270f00e-620c-53b0-82cf-ea6d2e6d169b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624801} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8f3f73-c92e-5e9c-a181-ee9fad1c30bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1270f00e-620c-53b0-82cf-ea6d2e6d169b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624801} :answer-field/id #uuid "6561f578-3b95-5931-8a50-3584ec7395a2" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{2}{3}x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192c9b37-1a1f-5454-922a-825b07a3d549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624803} {:answer/id #uuid "2da5b28f-17d1-541c-b3b4-b2d5655e3db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192c9b37-1a1f-5454-922a-825b07a3d549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624803} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a3a07d-44a9-5ca1-896b-b834ca0f2b29" :answer-field/key "$y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8c03d59-eacf-5f7a-bb18-0f76f1a5d12b" :question/problem "![](images/77/776ef945cb188befda6d6479bf10120428e9b77efcd4634c9bec02ecf4134cfc.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,1)$ and $(3,-1)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/2f/2f534e895418435f613e47853d84c692fce0281cd1f11bfe4779c84d33712f46.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1) &=\\frac{2}{3}(0)+1 \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=\\frac{2}{3}(3)+1 \\\\ -1 &=3\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $2y-\\frac{4}{3}x=2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)-\\frac{4}{3}(0) &=2 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ 2(-1)-\\frac{4}{3}(3) &=2 \\\\ -6 &=2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2y-\\frac{4}{3}x=2$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1) &=1-\\frac{2}{3}(0) \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=1-\\frac{2}{3}(3) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef1b9ae-7126-56d5-baa9-b20f87a08cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624826} {:answer/id #uuid "e2dd2fe2-9987-549f-9d23-fc35b34b236f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2dd2fe2-9987-549f-9d23-fc35b34b236f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624842} :answer-field/id #uuid "8263c959-51f7-5d3d-8c43-be6ccd1df0a0" :answer-field/key "$y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47a631e9-9670-5c0c-ac57-4ae3fb775d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624811} {:answer/id #uuid "47d399b6-ac89-5a80-b0bb-554849d5c25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47d399b6-ac89-5a80-b0bb-554849d5c25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624812} :answer-field/id #uuid "c381b027-e8e4-50a0-9be8-62cb031c1c16" :answer-field/key "$2y-3x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c18d31a-cc19-57b2-90c7-f599c0c66e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624818} {:answer/id #uuid "caea7151-5d36-5bb5-874b-89fb58d5369b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caea7151-5d36-5bb5-874b-89fb58d5369b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624834} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb96b7b-7963-5616-9a2f-9a347bf062fe" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{2}{3}x-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f282ccdc-a340-5563-90cb-3edb0578b2ab" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a49ee497281145f15b2ba053557e1f783ec98f9cd41f83a8d77ec3ddf8c60813.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(2,2)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/11/11926789df1b1240bb41a88bddc7fea03f81e1f23f813add7de979b3afe777fa.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=\\frac{2}{3}(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (2) &=\\frac{2}{3}(2)-1 \\\\ 2 &=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $2y-3x=-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)-3(0) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ 2(2)-3(2) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2y-3x=-2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=-1+\\frac{3}{2}(0) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (2) &=-1+\\frac{3}{2}(2) \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $2y-3x=-2$, $y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70b98ffb-80cb-5ca4-bd4c-259be4760585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624819} {:answer/id #uuid "d3750699-e025-55fe-a799-cf86276cb98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70b98ffb-80cb-5ca4-bd4c-259be4760585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624819} :answer-field/id #uuid "80bc88b4-25c2-5f15-9746-21faf2ee8e90" :answer-field/key "$y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "518a4bdb-8dcd-5207-b502-4aafcf9a9acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624813} {:answer/id #uuid "e719501a-040e-5570-af42-99c67304a516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "518a4bdb-8dcd-5207-b502-4aafcf9a9acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624813} :answer-field/id #uuid "c531402c-f61a-5f5d-9748-d54b2a954344" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1e069e5-16e7-52c3-97c9-97869e2457a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624827} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c149a1-4dac-5c62-bb14-a83c5383c8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1e069e5-16e7-52c3-97c9-97869e2457a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624827} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8c159f9-9229-5bd8-91dc-863dea7f745b" :answer-field/key "$y=-3-\\frac{2}{3}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8ed05a3-a2f1-5d93-9961-f5cdb8afd0d8" :question/problem "![](images/58/58fe55d2d673fb6ad2335444e6b704a7139b591304ee4fa883bfd37adb295661.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-3)$ and $(2,-6)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/75/75097de1c2a2d54e75ddbc626f01da74ad6fd21bc6d1d57eb5bc4b06a6fd8bcc.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(2,-6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(0)-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-6) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(2)-3 \\\\ -6 &=-6\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-3-\\frac{2}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(2,-6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=-3-\\frac{2}{3}(0) \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-6) &=-3-\\frac{2}{3}(2) \\\\ -6 &=- \\frac{13}{3}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3-\\frac{2}{3}x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(2,-6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)+\\frac{2}{3}(0) &=-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-6)+\\frac{2}{3}(2) &=-3 \\\\ - \\frac{14}{3} &=-3\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13445-0218-5950-967e-a68bcfec32c7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "156a008e-474a-5604-aa69-09adecd01936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626909} {:answer/id #uuid "df96de06-fac4-56a6-9520-765f12f1e56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df96de06-fac4-56a6-9520-765f12f1e56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626937} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b38b773-d846-509a-aa6f-3f9b6638f09f" :answer-field/key "$E=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -6 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 9 & 0.2 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 8 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22780c11-5c35-5927-991b-91567d8459b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626912} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0edfe3-d48b-57a7-b6ee-8a258f5fa041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e0edfe3-d48b-57a7-b6ee-8a258f5fa041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626927} :answer-field/id #uuid "a670f559-571c-5234-96fc-a2fa3ac41728" :answer-field/key "$T=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0.2 & 0.2 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ -5 & -10 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0.2 & -\\sqrt{2} & 10 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626934} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2862ae6e-3061-51ad-ac94-60cdc57569e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626915} {:answer/id #uuid "ec45720f-30d6-539e-ba0e-e1530203a466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2862ae6e-3061-51ad-ac94-60cdc57569e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626915} :answer-field/id #uuid "c17f608e-7d4a-5cbc-ab9f-6b38fdcf2145" :answer-field/key "$M=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cea5c3af-160c-5ad8-9a58-8a54d3d98908" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- $E$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $4$ rows and $4$ columns, so it is a $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- $M$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $T$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $4$ rows and $4$ columns, so it is a $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, $E$, $M$, and $T$ are square matrices."}]
